# earlyoom on the Galaxy M20: the second line behind MGLRU's min_ttl. When RAM
# and zram both run out (under 5 % available and under 10 % of swap free) it
# ends the process the kernel would pick, which ztMETRO makes the app least
# recently in front (oom_score_adj 300-900), before the kernel stalls.
# Never the shell, the login, sound or the system's own services.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 5 -s 10 -r 0 --avoid ^(ztmetro|greetd|pipewire|pipewire-pulse|wireplumber|systemd|systemd-.*|dbus-broker.*|sshd|NetworkManager|wpa_supplicant|Xwayland)$"
